    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:1e1fcafafd438aa8",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "cb2c4c360ebef92b65377b84c65f580e7e8cb0d1f1b732cd338cbe589aac8fa0",
      "text": "After breakfast, you will set off on an excursion to Machu Picchu with an English-speaking guide. The train follows the Urubamba River, then a winding road climbs to the ancient city among green peaks.\n\nThe terraces of Machu Picchu are arranged like steps on the slope. They held the soil in place, drained water and made it possible to use land where an ordinary field would have been impossible. During the tour, you will walk through squares, stairways, residential areas and temple precincts. In many places, the stone blocks fit so closely that the joints are barely visible.\n\nAfter the tour, you will have lunch and return to Cusco by train.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada_en_mw25u3yr",
        "model": "GPT-6",
        "wordAbsenceReason": "The Word Machu Picchu paragraph lacks the RU terrace engineering explanation and the assigned sequence of squares, stairways and residential/temple areas; translate the complete RU block with the agreed guide-language adaptation."
      }
